sequenceDiagram
    actor Student
    participant Client as Web client
    participant Backend
    participant Redis
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant Judge as DOMjudge
    actor Teacher as Teacher dashboard

    rect rgb(255, 248, 190)
        Note over Student,Teacher: Scenario A: submit a solution
        Student->>Client: Press "Submit"
        Client->>Backend: POST /contests/{id}/submissions
        Backend->>Backend: Check role, contest running, time left
        Backend->>DB: Store submission (verdict = pending)
        Backend->>Judge: POST submission (REST API)
        Judge-->>Backend: Submission id
        Backend-->>Client: 202 Accepted
        loop Until final verdict
            Client->>Backend: GET /submissions/{id}
            Backend->>Judge: Get judgement
            Judge-->>Backend: Verdict
            Backend->>DB: Update verdict
            Backend-->>Client: Verdict
        end
    end

    rect rgb(255, 248, 190)
        Note over Student,Teacher: Scenario B: integrity event
        Student->>Client: Switches to another tab
        Client->>Client: visibilitychange detected
        Client-->>Student: Show warning
        Client->>Backend: POST /contests/{id}/events (batch)
        Backend->>Backend: Validate event and participant
        Backend->>DB: Store event with server time
        Backend->>Backend: Recalculate risk score
        Backend->>Redis: Publish event and score
        Redis-->>Backend: Message for monitoring hub
        Backend-->>Teacher: WebSocket push (violation, new score)
    end
